{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"entry 3479584781 October 16 otelgin context restore behavior current correct pass context spawned goroutines Damien Tyler #8014","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"42b509db2d6a0a72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4091734457141958, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2543027810202797, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77053833, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu:**\\n\\n    *   Respond to the \\\"otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace\\\" issue/PR ([https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014)), suggesting passing context to spawned Go routines.\\n\\n    *   Follow up with Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives) regarding inactivity; if no response within a couple of weeks, initiate the process to move him to Emeritus status.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn:**\\n\\n    *   Draft a cohesive comment and close the \\\"Exposed Temporality Selector Function\\\" PR.\\n\\n    *   Review Robert Pająk's parsing algorithm PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)).\\n\\n    *   Add David Ashpole's metrics SDK optimization PRs (histogram reservoir, last value) to the current milestone.\\n\\n*   **All Attendees:**\\n\\n    *   Review Robert Pająk's parsing algorithm PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)).\\n\\n    *   Review David Ashpole's metrics SDK optimization PRs (especially the histogram reservoir one).\\n\\n    *   Prioritize reviews for critical PRs to facilitate a release before KubeCon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k action item damien mathieu respond to the otelgin context revers in datarac issu pr http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 suggest pass context to spawn go routin follow up with chengzhen scorpion knife regard inact if no respons within a coupl of week initi the process to move him to emeritus status tyler yahn draft a cohes comment and close the expos tempor selector function pr review robert paj ą k s pars algorithm pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 add david ashpol s metric sdk optim pr histogram reservoir last valu to the current mileston all attende review robert paj ą k s pars algorithm pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 review david ashpol s metric sdk optim pr especi the histogram reservoir one priorit review for critic pr to facilit a releas befor kubecon\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"e517eef4fe16eb1e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3835376348801974, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22281654982885343, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7585535, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Defer Provides No Benefit\\n\\nLet's analyze what the current code does:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() {\\n\\n      c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Restores AFTER request completes\\n\\n  }()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, propagation.HeaderCarrier(c.Request.Header))\\n\\n  // ...\\n\\n  c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // ← Sets new context\\n\\n  c.Next()  // ← Processes request\\n\\n  // When we return, defer runs and \\\"restores\\\" the old context\\n\\n```\\n\\n  Question: Why restore the context after the request is complete?\\n\\n  - After c.Next() returns, the request has been fully processed\\n\\n  - Gin doesn't reuse *gin.Context instances across requests\\n\\n  - Downstream handlers may spawn goroutines that read c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  - The deferred write to c.Request races with those goroutine reads\\n\\n  - There is no code that benefits from this restoration\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Performance Argument is Backwards\\n\\nThe current code with the defer is slower than the fix:\\n\\n  Current code overhead:\\n\\n  - Allocates closure for defer\\n\\n  - Saves context reference\\n\\n  - Executes deferred function on return\\n\\n  - Calls WithContext() twice (once to set, once to \\\"restore\\\")\\n\\n  Fixed code:\\n\\n  - No defer\\n\\n  - No closure allocation\\n\\n  - One fewer WithContext() call\\n\\n  - No unnecessary context copy\\n\\n Benchmark comparison (removing defer should show improvement):\\n\\n  -  Current: ~3 allocations per request\\n\\n  -  Fixed:   ~2 allocations per request\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"label mileston the defer provid no benefit let s analyz what the current code doe go savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx restor after request complet ctx cfg propag extract savedctx propag headercarri c request header c request c request withcontext ctx set new context c next process request when we return defer run and restor the old context question whi restor the context after the request is complet after c next return the request ha been fulli process gin doesn t reus gin context instanc across request downstream handler may spawn goroutin that read c request context the defer write to c request race with those goroutin read there is no code that benefit from this restor sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the perform argument is backward the current code with the defer is slower than the fix current code overhead alloc closur for defer save context refer execut defer function on return call withcontext twice onc to set onc to restor fix code no defer no closur alloc one fewer withcontext call no unnecessari context copi benchmark comparison remov defer should show improv current 3 alloc per request fix 2 alloc per request\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"088753f236e513b3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30636237531674326, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11656880045249043, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74921405, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455)\\n\\n*   **Bryan Boreham** questioned the relevance to OpenTelemetry, to which Damien clarified it's for instrumenting file uploads via the HTTP server.\\n\\n*   The discussion revolved around implementing an automatic cleanup mechanism for these temporary files. Proposed solutions included:\\n\\n    *   Option 1: `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`\\n\\n    *   Option 2: Leave it to the user to decide (\\\"whoever uses it is responsible for cleanup\\\")\\n\\n    *   Option 3: Provide a configurable option with a default.\\n\\n*   Damien suggested starting with automatic deletion without an explicit option, adding one only if a strong need arises. The notes from the agenda suggested starting with default behavior of removal, waiting for user interest to add configuration, and empowering component owners to make this decision.\\n\\n*   Tyler acknowledged that the instrumentation is responsible for cleanup and that this issue needs to be addressed.\\n\\n**3. Long-seen Code Owners/Triagers Check-in**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** reported that Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives), a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho, has had no GitHub activity since February and is the sole owner for otelecho.\\n\\n*   Damien pinged Chengzhen on Slack today and will wait a couple of weeks for a response. If there's no response, he plans to propose moving Chengzhen to Emeritus status due to inactivity.\\n\\n**4. Robert Pająk's PR (Parsing Algorithm)**\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** asked Tyler if his PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)) needed Tyler's specific review or if another approval would suffice to unblock it.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** encouraged others to review and stated that the project shouldn't be blocked waiting for him, though he would try to review it within a few days.\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** offered to review the PR. The goal is to merge it into the current milestone.\\n\\n**5. David Ashpole's PRs (Metrics SDK Optimizations)**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** provided an update on his histogram reservoir optimization PR. He explained that fixing a race condition initially worsened performance, making it equivalent to using a lock. The new approach involves one lock per measurement instead of one for the whole reservoir, resulting in a 3x-4x performance improvement. The PR is now much simpler and mostly involves concurrent safety testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 74455 http github com golang go issu 74455 bryan boreham question the relev to opentelemetri to which damien clarifi it s for instrument file upload via the http server the discuss revolv around implement an automat cleanup mechan for these temporari file propos solut includ option 1 c request multipartform removeal option 2 leav it to the user to decid whoever us it is respons for cleanup option 3 provid a configur option with a default damien suggest start with automat delet without an explicit option ad one onli if a strong need aris the note from the agenda suggest start with default behavior of remov wait for user interest to add configur and empow compon owner to make this decis tyler acknowledg that the instrument is respons for cleanup and that this issu need to be address 3 long seen code owner triager check in damien mathieu report that chengzhen scorpion knife a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho ha had no github activ sinc februari and is the sole owner for otelecho damien ping chengzhen on slack today and will wait a coupl of week for a respons if there s no respons he plan to propos move chengzhen to emeritus status due to inact 4 robert paj ą k s pr pars algorithm robert paj ą k ask tyler if his pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 need tyler s specif review or if anoth approv would suffic to unblock it tyler yahn encourag other to review and state that the project shouldn t be block wait for him though he would tri to review it within a few day david ashpol offer to review the pr the goal is to merg it into the current mileston 5 david ashpol s pr metric sdk optim david ashpol provid an updat on his histogram reservoir optim pr he explain that fix a race condit initi worsen perform make it equival to use a lock the new approach involv one lock per measur instead of one for the whole reservoir result in a 3x 4x perform improv the pr is now much simpler and most involv concurr safeti test\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"287e2a602b3808f0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3058603465375114, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12087158076787344, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7375008, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"50410b2f868e71d1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30224976939974413, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1008256848567773, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7722393, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```go\\n\\nfunc Middleware() {\\n\\n    savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    defer func() {\\n\\n        c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Step 5: WRITE\\n\\n    }()\\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // Step 1\\n\\n    c.Next()                                 // Step 2: All handlers/middleware run\\n\\n    // Step 3: Handler spawned goroutine that reads c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    // Step 4: Handler returns\\n\\n    // Step 5: defer runs and WRITES to c.Request\\n\\n    // Step 6: Background goroutine READS c.Request ← **RACE**!\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nThe defer IS the concurrent modification. It writes to c.Request after handlers complete, while\\n\\nbackground goroutines spawned by those handlers may still be reading it.\\n\\nThe fix removes this write:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nfunc Middleware() {\\n\\n    reqCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(reqCtx, ...)\\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // Step 1: Set once\\n\\n    c.Next()                                 // Step 2: Handlers run\\n\\n    // Step 3: Handler spawns goroutine\\n\\n    // Step 4: Handler returns\\n\\n    // Step 5: No defer, no write ← NO RACE\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nProof: TestMiddleware_MinimalRaceRepro demonstrates exactly this:\\n\\n- Handler spawns goroutine that accesses c.Request.Context()\\n\\n- Handler returns\\n\\n- Old code: defer writes → DATA RACE\\n\\n- Fixed code: no write → PASS\\n\\nFurthermore this isn't my \\\"specific case\\\" - this is how Go middleware is supposed to work. The defer breaks standard Go patterns that every Go developer uses.\\n\\nGo's own documentation recommends this pattern\\n\\nFrom https://pkg.go.dev/context:\\n\\n>   \\\"Incoming requests to a server should create a Context, and outgoing calls to servers should accept a Context. The chain of function calls between them must propagate the Context,\\n\\n>   optionally replacing it with a derived Context...\\\"\\n\\n> \\n\\nPassing c.Request.Context() to goroutines is the recommended approach for:\\n\\n  - Timeouts\\n\\n  - Cancellation\\n\\n  - Tracing (which is what otelgin does!)\\n\\nOther popular Gin middleware use this exact pattern!\\n\\nExample using an extremely common pattern in production:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n func main() {\\n\\n      router := gin.New()\\n\\n      // Setup OpenTelemetry tracing (standard pattern)\\n\\n      router.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-service\\\"))\\n\\n      // Add async logging middleware (also standard pattern)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"go func middlewar savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx step 5 write c request c request withcontext ctx step 1 c next step 2 all handler middlewar run step 3 handler spawn goroutin that read c request context step 4 handler return step 5 defer run and write to c request step 6 background goroutin read c request race the defer is the concurr modif it write to c request after handler complet while background goroutin spawn by those handler may still be read it the fix remov this write go func middlewar reqctx c request context ctx cfg propag extract reqctx c request c request withcontext ctx step 1 set onc c next step 2 handler run step 3 handler spawn goroutin step 4 handler return step 5 no defer no write no race proof testmiddlewar _ minimalracerepro demonstr exact this handler spawn goroutin that access c request context handler return old code defer write data race fix code no write pas furthermor this isn t my specif case this is how go middlewar is suppos to work the defer break standard go pattern that everi go develop us go s own document recommend this pattern from http pkg go dev context incom request to a server should creat a context and outgo call to server should accept a context the chain of function call between them must propag the context option replac it with a deriv context pass c request context to goroutin is the recommend approach for timeout cancel trace which is what otelgin doe other popular gin middlewar use this exact pattern exampl use an extrem common pattern in product go func main router gin new setup opentelemetri trace standard pattern router use otelgin middlewar my servic add async log middlewar also standard pattern\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"41e8d21fecc0b159\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29648637203874384, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10607339005534833, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74078333, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThere seems to be absolutely no reason to save and restore the request context in a deferred function. The way it was done before could (and did) lead to a race condition because when c.Next() is called, the request context could be changed by another goroutine, and then the deferred function would modify the request while another goroutine is using it. \\n\\nI can't for the life of me figure out what benefit the previous code was trying to achieve, other than maybe trying to minimize the context size in memory, but that seems unnecessary and not worth the risk of a data race. Furthermore, I'm not even sure that said memory savings would pay off because when running `go build -gcflags=\\\"-m\\\"` against the current implementation you can see that context and request escapes to heap:\\n\\n```\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: \\\"nil context\\\" escapes to heap\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: new(http.Request) escapes to heap\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis is likely negligible but I figured I'd add it for more context, no pun intended 😉\\n\\nPerhaps the goal was not that of performance/memory savings but instead to \\\"restore\\\" the context. If so, this is also incorrect because in Gin, there's no need to restore the context - each request gets its own *gin.Context .\\n\\nFinally, this change actually more closely matches the [code cited](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go/blob/8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6/contrib/gin-gonic/gin/gintrace.go) as the \\\"inspiration\\\" for the otelgin package. \\n\\nWithout this change, we unfortunately cannot run our tests with the race detector enabled and is not production ready due to not being goroutine safe.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston descript there seem to be absolut no reason to save and restor the request context in a defer function the way it wa done befor could and did lead to a race condit becaus when c next is call the request context could be chang by anoth goroutin and then the defer function would modifi the request while anoth goroutin is use it i can t for the life of me figur out what benefit the previous code wa tri to achiev other than mayb tri to minim the context size in memori but that seem unnecessari and not worth the risk of a data race furthermor i m not even sure that said memori save would pay off becaus when run go build gcflag m against the current implement you can see that context and request escap to heap gin go 84 37 nil context escap to heap gin go 84 37 new http request escap to heap this is like neglig but i figur i d add it for more context no pun intend perhap the goal wa not that of perform memori save but instead to restor the context if so this is also incorrect becaus in gin there s no need to restor the context each request get it own gin context final this chang actual more close match the code cite http github com datadog dd trace go blob 8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6 contrib gin gonic gin gintrac go a the inspir for the otelgin packag without this chang we unfortun can not run our test with the race detector enabl and is not product readi due to not be goroutin safe\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"1da5f5d80dd66eac\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2934860341217446, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09033027445963518, \"vector_similarity\": 0.76751614, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 43 31z just found an open 2 year old issu this would fix 4588 nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 56 41z thank for the quick respons flc1125 but i would like to offer a rebutt sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston this pr fix an exist bug not introduc new safeti mechan i respect disagre with the character that this pr introduc mechan for concurr safeti the opposit is true this pr remov problemat code that caus a data race the current code ha a real reproduc race condit report in issu 4588 open for 2 year the race detector fail consist this is not theoret it violat go s memori model sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"09feab0883dcf7bb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28610350484374514, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07983486406249309, \"vector_similarity\": 0.767397, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I'm not quite sure about your specific case, so this is for reference only: Since `*http.Request` is often passed to subsequent logic, if there are concurrent modifications to it, it can lead to thread safety issues.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-10-14T05:13:28Z\\n\\n> > I'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race` in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I'm not quite sure about your specific case, so this is for reference only: Since `*http.Request` is often passed to subsequent logic, if there are concurrent modifications to it, it can lead to thread safety issues.\\n\\n That’s essentially what’s happening here, this would be an example of subsequent logic that’s creating a data race. We can’t guarantee that others middleware’s won’t do something similar but I think this is a valid fix.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:13:48Z\\n\\n  The \\\"hygiene to avoid leaking modifications\\\" argument is backwards. The defer causes the race, it doesn't prevent leaking:\\n\\n  1. There's nothing to leak - Gin doesn't reuse *gin.Context across requests. Each request gets a fresh context.\\n\\n  2. The defer IS the race - When a handler spawns a goroutine that reads c.Request.Context(), the defer writes to c.Request while that goroutine reads from it. That's the data race.\\n\\n  3. Proof:\\n\\n  ```go\\n\\n  router.POST(\\\"/test\\\", func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n      ctx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n      go func() {\\n\\n          time.Sleep(1ms)\\n\\n          _ = ctx.Value(\\\"key\\\")  // READ\\n\\n      }()\\n\\n      c.JSON(200, \\\"ok\\\")\\n\\n      // defer runs here and WRITES to c.Request ← RACE!\\n\\n  })\\n\\n  ```\\n\\nThe \\\"concurrent modifications\\\" concern is the problem we're fixing - The defer itself is the concurrent modification! It writes to c.Request after the handler returns while background goroutines may still be using it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:19:18Z\\n\\n Here's a test you can run to test this for yourself. It proves the current implementation is the culprit for data races.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i m not quit sure about your specif case so this is for refer onli sinc http request is often pass to subsequ logic if there are concurr modif to it it can lead to thread safeti issu akats7 2025 10 14t05 13 28z i m confus about this doesn t provid thread safeti claim i m star at a test failur due to data race when run go test race in one of my project that clear point the finger to the code i remov a be the culprit when i do a go mod replac use my chang in this pr the race go away i m not quit sure about your specif case so this is for refer onli sinc http request is often pass to subsequ logic if there are concurr modif to it it can lead to thread safeti issu that s essenti what s happen here this would be an exampl of subsequ logic that s creat a data race we can t guarante that other middlewar s won t do someth similar but i think this is a valid fix nicksherron 2025 10 14t05 13 48z the hygien to avoid leak modif argument is backward the defer caus the race it doesn t prevent leak 1 there s noth to leak gin doesn t reus gin context across request each request get a fresh context 2 the defer is the race when a handler spawn a goroutin that read c request context the defer write to c request while that goroutin read from it that s the data race 3 proof go router post test func c gin context ctx c request context go func time sleep 1ms _ ctx valu key read c json 200 ok defer run here and write to c request race the concurr modif concern is the problem we re fix the defer itself is the concurr modif it write to c request after the handler return while background goroutin may still be use it nicksherron 2025 10 14t05 19 18z here s a test you can run to test this for yourself it prof the current implement is the culprit for data race\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"a65f1a1d2683f03e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28402121576074435, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09557797965820623, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7237221, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Users Cannot Fix This Themselves\\n\\n This is middleware code that users cannot work around without forking the library. The race happens inside otelgin.Middleware(). A user who wants to use otelgin AND pass race detection has no choice but to:\\n\\n  1. Fork this library\\n\\n  2. Apply this exact fix\\n\\n  3. Maintain their fork indefinitely\\n\\n  This is not \\\"leaving the decision to users\\\"—it's forcing users to fork or live with failing race detection.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Precedent: This Project Has Fixed Similar Races Before\\n\\n  From the git history:\\n\\n  - #4577: \\\"otelgrpc: Fix data race in stats handlers\\\" (merged)\\n\\n  - #881: \\\"otelsarama: Fix WrapAsyncProducer race condition\\\" (merged)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston user can not fix this themselv this is middlewar code that user can not work around without fork the librari the race happen insid otelgin middlewar a user who want to use otelgin and pas race detect ha no choic but to 1 fork this librari 2 appli this exact fix 3 maintain their fork indefinit this is not leav the decis to user it s forc user to fork or live with fail race detect sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston preced this project ha fix similar race befor from the git histori 4577 otelgrpc fix data race in stat handler merg 881 otelsarama fix wrapasyncproduc race condit merg\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"567b1a3caf312d89\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28391544284374515, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07983486406249309, \"vector_similarity\": 0.76010346, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074c61ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"entry 3479584781 October 16 otelgin context restore behavior current correct pass context spawned goroutines Damien Tyler #8014\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"PR **#8014 was closed without merging** because the Go SIG decided the existing context-restoration behavior was intentional and correct.\n\nOn 2025-10-16, Damien Mathieu and Tyler Yahn concluded that code starting goroutines should explicitly pass the needed context/span into them, rather than rely on `otelgin` leaving its derived context attached after middleware returns. Tyler also favored linked spans for asynchronous work over making those goroutines children of the request span. The PR was then closed on 2025-10-17. `(WS-05/T007; SRC-NOTE-04; SRC-PR-07)`\n\nSo, although the PR author presented the deferred restore as a reproducible data-race source, the maintainers’ decision was a semantic/design one: retain context reversal and require explicit context propagation for asynchronous work."}}
